---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import OrbStage from '../../components/OrbStage.astro';
import { downloads } from '../../config/downloads';
---

<Base
  title="Niyora vs Stardust: predict your PMS window and get through it · Niyora"
  description="Stardust is an astrology-flavored cycle tracker built around logging and predictions, then it stops. Niyora predicts your PMS window too, then helps you through it: reflect, regulate, respond in about a minute, plus training that builds the skill. No account."
  canonicalUrl="https://niyora.com/compare/niyora-vs-stardust/"
>
  <OrbStage />

  <main class="content">
    <section class="hero" data-hue="255" data-sat="60%">
      <div class="eyebrow">Niyora vs Stardust</div>
      <h1>Stardust tracks your cycle. Niyora helps you through the hard hour.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Stardust is a cycle tracker with an astrology flavor. You log, it learns your pattern, it tells you what is coming, and there it stops. Niyora tracks and predicts your PMS window too, but it does not stop at the prediction. When the feeling actually lands, it helps you reflect, regulate, and respond in about a minute, and its training builds the skill before you need it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="moat-section" data-hue="250" data-sat="58%">
      <div class="moat">
        <p>A tracker tells you it is coming, then leaves you to handle it. Niyora predicts the same window, then <strong>shows up when it lands</strong>: reflect, regulate, respond in about a minute, and training that builds the skill before you need it. The prediction is where a tracker finishes. For Niyora it is where the help starts.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="table-section" data-hue="290" data-sat="55%">
      <h2>The difference, line by line</h2>
      <div class="compare-grid">
        <div class="compare-head them">A cycle tracker like Stardust</div>
        <div class="compare-head us">Niyora</div>

        <div class="compare-cell them"><p>Logs and predicts your cycle in an astrology-tinged story. Once it predicts, its job is done.</p></div>
        <div class="compare-cell us"><p>Tracks and predicts your window too, then walks you through reflect, regulate, respond when it lands.</p></div>

        <div class="compare-cell them"><p>You feed it data, and the prediction is the finish line.</p></div>
        <div class="compare-cell us"><p>Training builds the skill before the window, so it lands lighter when it comes.</p></div>

        <div class="compare-cell them"><p>Emotional support is a themed reading tied to where you are in your cycle.</p></div>
        <div class="compare-cell us"><p>A way to see the moment differently, settle your body, and respond without regret.</p></div>

        <div class="compare-cell them"><p>Success is a more complete record of you over time.</p></div>
        <div class="compare-cell us"><p>Success is you moving through the moment, and needing it less.</p></div>

        <div class="compare-cell them"><p>Covers the whole cycle across every phase and mood.</p></div>
        <div class="compare-cell us"><p>Built for one window only. The days before your period, when feelings run high.</p></div>

        <div class="compare-cell them"><p>Your cycle data lives in an account so it can predict across time.</p></div>
        <div class="compare-cell us"><p>No account, no sign in. Your personal details are stripped before anything reaches the AI.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="honest-section" data-hue="278" data-sat="55%">
      <div class="honest">
        <h2>To be fair to Stardust</h2>
        <p>A tracker with a distinct voice can make logging feel less clinical, and plenty of people enjoy that. Niyora tracks and predicts too, so this is not tracker versus no tracker. The difference is what happens after the prediction: Stardust hands you a date, Niyora helps you through the days it points to. Many people will happily use both.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section" data-hue="30" data-sat="70%">
      <h2>Not sure the hard week is even PMS?</h2>
      <p class="lede">Take the two-minute check and see how your premenstrual week actually hits.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/quiz" class="cta">Take the quiz</a>
        <a href={downloads.appStore} class="cta ghost">Get Niyora</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <a href="/compare/alternatives-to-mood-trackers/">Alternatives to mood trackers</a>
    <a href="/blog/">Writing</a>
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
    <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>
    <div class="copyright">© 2026 Niyora. Built quietly in Norway.</div>
  </footer>
</Base>

<style>
  .content { position: relative; z-index: 2; }

  section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 72px 40px;
    max-width: 1080px;
    margin: 26px auto;
    border-radius: 32px;
    background: rgba(12, 10, 20, 0.24);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    backdrop-filter: blur(16px) saturate(1.15);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px) saturate(1.15);
    box-shadow: 0 24px 70px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34);
    text-align: center;
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    section { margin: 14px; border-radius: 24px; padding: 56px 20px; }
  }

  .hero { padding: 96px 40px 80px; }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 4px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 50%, 75%, 0.7);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    transition: color 1.4s ease;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 48px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.16;
    letter-spacing: -0.5px;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    max-width: 780px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.3px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    max-width: 720px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);
  }
  p { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 300; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.66); max-width: 640px; }
  p.lede { font-size: 20px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.74); line-height: 1.55; }

  .moat {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding: 32px 30px;
    border-radius: 20px;
    border: 1px solid hsla(var(--orb-hue), 55%, 60%, 0.3);
    background: var(--glass-bg);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow);
  }
  .moat p { font-size: 21px; font-weight: 300; line-height: 1.5; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.86); max-width: none; margin: 0; }
  .moat strong { color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 84%, 0.98); font-weight: 500; }

  .compare-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 900px;
    text-align: left;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .compare-head {
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 3px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .compare-head.them { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4); }
  .compare-head.us { color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 80%, 0.95); transition: color 1.4s ease; }
  .compare-cell {
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    border: 1px solid var(--glass-border);
    background: var(--glass-bg-soft);
    box-shadow: var(--glass-shadow);
    backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur);
  }
  .compare-cell p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; margin: 0; max-width: none; }
  .compare-cell.them { background: rgba(20, 18, 26, 0.35); }
  .compare-cell.them p { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5); }
  .compare-cell.us { border-color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 55%, 60%, 0.35); }
  .compare-cell.us p { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .compare-grid { gap: 10px 12px; }
    .compare-cell { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }

  .honest { max-width: 680px; }
  .honest p { margin: 0 auto; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; }

  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; margin-top: 12px; }
  .cta {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 16px 36px;
    border-radius: 32px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
    color: rgba(18, 16, 32, 0.95);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.3px;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease, background 0.3s ease, color 0.3s ease;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 32px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 55%, 0.35), 0 0 64px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 60%, 60%, 0.2);
  }
  .cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px) scale(1.02);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1);
    color: hsla(var(--orb-hue), 70%, 32%, 1);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 80%, 70%, 0.45), 0 14px 48px hsla(var(--orb-hue), 80%, 60%, 0.75);
  }
  .cta.ghost {
    background: transparent;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22);
    box-shadow: none;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
  }
  .cta.ghost:hover { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5); color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1); }

  footer {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 60px 24px 80px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.3);
    font-size: 13px;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  footer a { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45); text-decoration: none; margin: 0 14px; }
  footer a:hover { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); }
  footer .copyright { margin-top: 16px; font-size: 12px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    h1 { font-size: 34px; }
    h2 { font-size: 26px; }
    p.lede { font-size: 17px; }
    .moat p { font-size: 18px; }
  }
</style>
</parameter>
</invoke>
